Hi all,

I’m trying to use a background image and overlay geocoded map points. The code below works fine except that annotation_custom () won’t work with coord_map(). The code below shows ##coord_map(), but that means that the geocoding is off. I’m using a .png file, and while there’s a .svg file of the same map, I’m not sure using that would solve the problem. I’d appreciate any advice.

library(mapdata)
library(ggplot2)
library(ggmap)
library(png)
library(grid)

download.file("http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_of_the_Third_Century#mediaviewer/File:Map_of_Ancient_Rome_271_AD.svg", "Rome.svg")
download.file("http://history.emory.edu/RAVINA/1024px-Map_of_Ancient_Rome_271_AD.png", "Rome.png")
img <- readPNG("Rome.png")
back.map <- rasterGrob(img, interpolate=TRUE)
Italy <- geocode(c("Rome","Pisa"))
ggplot(Rome, aes(x=Italy$lon, y=Italy$lat)) +
  xlim(c(0,30)) +ylim(c(30,50))+
  ##coord_map() +
  annotation_custom(back.map, xmin=-Inf, xmax=Inf, ymin=-Inf, ymax=Inf) +
  geom_point()+
  ggtitle("Ancient Rome”)

Thanks,
Mark
Professor of History
Emory University
Editorial Board, Journal of Asian Studies

