A few modifications to your code produce what I think you want:

ggplot(data, aes(y=xcovariate_f, x=or, xmin=lc, xmax=uc))+
  geom_errorbarh(size = 1, height = 0)+
  geom_point(size = 2.5) +
  geom_vline(aes(y=0), lty=2) +
  geom_text(x = 0.2, aes(label= string.est,
                         y = as.numeric(xcovariate_f) - 0.5),
            size = 2.5, hjust = 0, colour="black")+
  facet_wrap(~ age_cat_f)+
  labs(x = "Adjusted hazard ratio (95% CI) ", y = NULL)+
  theme_bw() +
  theme(panel.grid.major=element_blank(),
        panel.grid.minor=element_blank(),
        strip.background = element_rect(colour="black",
                                        fill='white'))

The main culprit was the reference to data$xcovariate_f in geom_text(). I also changed geom_pointrange() to a combination of
geom_errorbarh() and geom_point() to avoid the need for a coord_flip(). As a result, the x's need to be changed to y's and vice versa in the plot code.

Dennis

